1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,076
这是一个医院数据库，每个病人一条记录
Here is a hospital database, one row per patient.

2
00:00:03,396 --> 00:00:08,668
有位研究者问了个看似无害的问题：有多少病人患有疾病 X？
A researcher asks an innocent question: how many patients have condition X?

3
00:00:08,989 --> 00:00:10,687
医院不公开任何记录
The hospital releases no records.

4
00:00:11,007 --> 00:00:13,076
它只给了一个数：41
It just says: 41.

5
00:00:13,317 --> 00:00:16,291
一周后，一位新病人 Alice 入院了
A week later, one new patient, Alice, is admitted.

6
00:00:16,611 --> 00:00:18,211
研究者又问了一遍
The researcher asks again.

7
00:00:18,423 --> 00:00:20,023
现在答案是 42
The answer is now 42.

8
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:24,627
两数一减，研究者就知道了 Alice 一件很具体的事
Subtract, and the researcher has learned something very specific about Alice,

9
00:00:24,627 --> 00:00:26,310
却一条记录都没看
without seeing a single record.

10
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:29,697
继续之前，先自己试着补上这个漏洞
Before we go on, try to fix this yourself.

11
00:00:30,017 --> 00:00:34,459
暂停想一想：人数四舍五入到十位，能保护 Alice 吗？
Pause and ponder: would rounding the count to the nearest ten protect Alice?

12
00:00:34,779 --> 00:00:37,954
需要多想一会儿的话，可以先暂停视频
Pause the video if you need more time.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,527
大多数星期里，确实可以
Most weeks, yes.

14
00:00:50,847 --> 00:00:53,461
但如果人数从 44 变成 45
But if the count goes from 44 to 45,

15
00:00:53,461 --> 00:00:58,171
取整后的答案就从 40 跳到 50，Alice 又暴露了
the rounded answer jumps from 40 to 50, and Alice is exposed again.

16
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:03,659
任何确定性的规则，只要答案会变，就一定在某处有这样的跳变
Any fixed rule that ever changes its answer has a jump like that somewhere.

17
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:07,524
那发布统计量，到底怎样才算不泄露隐私？
So what would it even mean for a statistic to be private?

18
00:01:07,844 --> 00:01:10,511
如果靠加噪声，那加多少才够？
And if the fix is to add noise, how much is enough?

19
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:14,116
2006 年，Cynthia Dwork、Frank McSherry
In 2006, Cynthia Dwork, Frank McSherry,

20
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:16,355
Kobbi Nissim 和 Adam Smith
Kobbi Nissim and Adam Smith

21
00:01:16,355 --> 00:01:18,690
在这篇 paper 里回答了这两个问题
answered both questions in this paper:

22
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:23,603
《Calibrating Noise to Sensitivity in Private Data Analysis》
Calibrating Noise to Sensitivity in Private Data Analysis.

23
00:01:23,923 --> 00:01:28,821
它开创了我们今天所说的差分隐私（differential privacy）
It founded what we now call differential privacy,

24
00:01:28,821 --> 00:01:31,270
2017 年还获得了哥德尔奖
and in 2017 it won the Gödel Prize.

25
00:01:31,517 --> 00:01:35,529
这期视频讲它的三个核心想法：隐私的定义
This video covers its three big ideas: a definition of privacy,

26
00:01:35,529 --> 00:01:38,748
一个数叫敏感度（sensitivity）
a number called sensitivity,

27
00:01:38,748 --> 00:01:41,958
以及一个公式，算噪声加多少才够
and a recipe for how much noise is enough.

28
00:01:42,278 --> 00:01:44,298
还有个出人意料的限制
Plus a surprising limit

29
00:01:44,298 --> 00:01:48,339
要满足这个定义，只公开一张表，能做的很有限
on what one published table can achieve, if it must be private in this sense.

30
00:01:49,783 --> 00:01:53,262
先画一张地图，看看这篇 paper 从哪儿来
First, a map of where this paper comes from.

31
00:01:53,582 --> 00:01:58,634
1965 年，Stanley Warner 为敏感问题调查提出了随机响应
In 1965, Stanley Warner proposed randomized response for sensitive surveys.

32
00:01:58,954 --> 00:02:01,919
在常见的版本里，你私下掷一枚硬币
In a popular version, you flip a coin in private.

33
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:04,154
正面，你就如实回答
Heads, you answer truthfully.

34
00:02:04,474 --> 00:02:08,523
反面，你就再掷一次：正面答“是”，反面答“否”
Tails, you flip again and say yes for heads, no for tails.

35
00:02:08,843 --> 00:02:12,334
任何一个“是”，都可能只是硬币替你说的
Any single yes could be the coin talking,

36
00:02:12,334 --> 00:02:15,988
但问上成千上万人，真实比例照样能估出来
yet over thousands of people the true rate can still be estimated.

37
00:02:16,308 --> 00:02:17,666
记住这枚硬币
Keep this coin in mind.

38
00:02:17,716 --> 00:02:22,937
之后几十年，统计学家和计算机科学家，不断改进这类 trick
Over the following decades, statisticians and computer scientists refined such tricks,

39
00:02:22,937 --> 00:02:27,917
分成两种思路：要么扰动输入的数据，要么扰动输出的答案
in two flavours: scramble the data going in, or scramble the answers coming out.

40
00:02:28,166 --> 00:02:33,670
与此同时，最容易想到的办法，也就是直接去掉姓名，却一再失败
Meanwhile, the obvious fix, just remove the names, kept failing.

41
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:36,267
Latanya Sweeney 发现
Latanya Sweeney showed

42
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:41,285
光凭邮编、出生日期和性别，就能唯一识别大多数美国人
that ZIP code, birth date and sex alone single out most Americans,

43
00:02:41,285 --> 00:02:46,254
1997 年，她把号称匿名的病历和公开的选民名单一对照
and in 1997 she linked supposedly anonymous hospital records to a public voter list

44
00:02:46,254 --> 00:02:48,569
就认出了马萨诸塞州州长
and found the governor of Massachusetts.

45
00:02:48,889 --> 00:02:52,444
教训是：隐私必须是发布过程本身的性质
The lesson: privacy must be a property of the process,

46
00:02:52,444 --> 00:02:55,250
而不是看发布出来的表长什么样
not of how the released table looks,

47
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:59,365
而且无论攻击者还知道什么，这一点都必须成立
and it must hold whatever else the attacker knows.

48
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,008
然后在 2003 年
Then, in 2003,

49
00:03:01,008 --> 00:03:05,714
Irit Dinur 和 Kobbi Nissim 证明了一个令人警醒的结论
Irit Dinur and Kobbi Nissim proved something sobering.

50
00:03:06,034 --> 00:03:09,913
问题答得太多、太准，误差远小于根号 n
Answer too many questions too accurately, with errors much smaller than the square root of n,

51
00:03:09,913 --> 00:03:13,162
攻击者就能重构出几乎整个数据库
and an attacker can rebuild almost the entire database.

52
00:03:13,482 --> 00:03:18,821
我们那个做减法的攻击，其实就是这种攻击只问两个问题的版本
Our subtraction was the two-question version of this attack.

53
00:03:19,141 --> 00:03:21,907
噪声，就是回答很多问题的代价
Noise is the price of answering many questions.

54
00:03:22,150 --> 00:03:26,721
反过来也有好消息：问题数量有限，适量噪声就够了
The hopeful flip side: with a limited number of questions, modest noise is enough.

55
00:03:27,041 --> 00:03:31,733
Dwork、Nissim 和合作者，据此做了个叫 SuLQ 的框架
Dwork, Nissim and colleagues built this into a framework called SuLQ,

56
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:34,616
意思是只问次线性数量的 query（查询）
for sub-linear queries,

57
00:03:34,616 --> 00:03:37,442
它回答带噪声的求和，比如人数
which answers noisy sums like counts.

58
00:03:37,762 --> 00:03:39,362
记住提问的上限
Remember that limit on questions.

59
00:03:39,497 --> 00:03:41,959
这篇 paper 把它变成一笔预算
This paper turns it into a budget.

60
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:44,430
但 SuLQ 只能处理求和
But SuLQ only covered sums,

61
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:48,574
而且它的定义允许有极小的概率发生大量泄露
and its definition tolerated a tiny chance of a large leak.

62
00:03:48,894 --> 00:03:53,285
这篇 paper 迈出了一大步：适用于数据的任意函数
This paper takes the leap: any function of the data,

63
00:03:53,285 --> 00:03:56,967
只用一个干净的定义和一条简单的噪声规则
one clean definition, and one simple rule for the noise.

64
00:03:57,287 --> 00:04:02,488
难怪它发表在密码学会议上：那里的习惯就是先定义安全性
Fittingly, it appeared at a cryptography conference, where the habit is to define security

65
00:04:02,488 --> 00:04:06,148
要求能抵御所有可能的攻击者，再去证明
against every possible attacker first, and then prove it.

66
00:04:08,583 --> 00:04:10,277
先交代一下 setting
Here is the setting.

67
00:04:10,597 --> 00:04:13,847
可信的服务器，也就是数据管理者
A trusted server, the curator,

68
00:04:13,847 --> 00:04:17,340
持有数据库 x：n 条记录，每人一条
holds a database x: n rows, one per person.

69
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,746
分析者发来 query f
An analyst sends a query f,

70
00:04:19,746 --> 00:04:23,555
数据库的任意函数，返回一个数或一组数
any function of the database that returns a number, or a list of numbers.

71
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:27,388
数据管理者从不公开真实答案 f(x)
The curator never releases the honest answer, f(x).

72
00:04:27,708 --> 00:04:32,659
它的做法是先抽一个随机噪声 Y，再公开 f(x) 加 Y
Instead it draws random noise, Y, and releases f(x) + Y.

73
00:04:32,979 --> 00:04:37,677
因为分析者可以一直问下去，所以这叫交互式的 setting
Because the analyst can keep asking, this is called the interactive setting.

74
00:04:37,997 --> 00:04:41,475
另一种做法是发布一张经过隐私处理的表
The alternative, publishing one sanitized table

75
00:04:41,475 --> 00:04:44,038
然后撒手不管，这叫非交互式
and walking away, is non-interactive.

76
00:04:44,358 --> 00:04:47,838
原文最后证明了，交互式从根本上更强
At the end, the paper proves the first is fundamentally more powerful.

77
00:04:48,083 --> 00:04:52,716
所以一切都归结到一个问题：Y 应该服从什么分布？
So everything hinges on one question: what distribution should Y have?

78
00:04:53,036 --> 00:04:55,528
噪声太少，Alice 就暴露了
Too little noise, and Alice is exposed.

79
00:04:55,848 --> 00:04:57,629
太多，答案就没用了
Too much, and the answer is useless.

80
00:04:57,949 --> 00:05:01,676
标题已经给出了答案：按敏感度校准噪声
The title gives the answer: calibrate the noise to the sensitivity.

81
00:05:01,996 --> 00:05:05,750
不过我们先要搞清楚：到底什么叫不泄露隐私？
But first, what does private actually mean?

82
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,755
关键是想象两个世界
The key move is to imagine two worlds.

83
00:05:09,075 --> 00:05:10,924
一边是数据库 x
In one, the database is x.

84
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:14,715
另一边是 x′：只有一条记录不同
In the other, it is x′: identical except for one row.

85
00:05:15,035 --> 00:05:16,650
比如 Alice 那条
Say, Alice's.

86
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:19,199
这样的一对叫相邻数据库（也叫相邻数据集）
Databases like this are called neighbors.

87
00:05:19,519 --> 00:05:23,390
医院例子里多了 Alice；这里是她的记录变了
In the hospital, Alice was added; here, her row just says something different.

88
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:26,490
总之，谁的记录都不该影响太大
Either way, no single person's row should matter much.

89
00:05:26,733 --> 00:05:30,454
把这个机制，也就是数据管理者随机作答的规则
Run the mechanism, the curator's randomized answering rule,

90
00:05:30,454 --> 00:05:32,314
在两个世界里各跑一次
in each world.

91
00:05:32,634 --> 00:05:36,409
分析者能看到的一切，原文叫 transcript（交互历史）
Whatever the analyst gets to see, the paper calls the transcript;

92
00:05:36,409 --> 00:05:38,856
目前就是一个带噪声的答案
for now, a single noisy answer.

93
00:05:39,176 --> 00:05:43,639
因为机制是随机的，每个世界都对应一个完整的输出分布
Because the mechanism is random, each world gives a whole distribution of possible outputs.

94
00:05:43,883 --> 00:05:47,631
任取一个输出 t，比较两条曲线在这里的高度
Pick any output t, and compare the heights of the two curves there.

95
00:05:47,951 --> 00:05:50,083
滑动 t，看它们的比值
Slide t along and watch their ratio.

96
00:05:50,403 --> 00:05:53,992
满足差分隐私的机制，让比值处处接近 1
A private mechanism keeps that ratio close to 1 everywhere:

97
00:05:53,992 --> 00:05:59,149
不超过 e^ε，也不低于 e^(−ε)
never above e^ε, never below e^(−ε).

98
00:05:59,383 --> 00:06:03,134
这就是原文的定义，叫作 ε-不可区分性（即 ε-差分隐私）
That is the paper's definition, which it calls ε-indistinguishability.

99
00:06:03,454 --> 00:06:06,855
比值的对数，就是输出 t 处的隐私损失
The log of the ratio is the privacy loss at t.

100
00:06:07,175 --> 00:06:11,401
对任意一对相邻数据库、任意分析者、任意输出
For every pair of neighbors, every analyst and every output,

101
00:06:11,401 --> 00:06:14,282
它的绝对值都不能超过 ε
it must be at most ε in absolute value.

102
00:06:14,602 --> 00:06:19,452
取绝对值就对称了：比值是 2 还是 1/2，都算一样
The absolute value makes it symmetric: a ratio of 2 and a ratio of 1/2 count the same.

103
00:06:19,772 --> 00:06:25,363
ε 很小的时候，e^ε 约等于 1 + ε
For small ε, e^ε is about 1 + ε.

104
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:27,914
拿地图上 Warner 的硬币试试
Let's test it on Warner's coin from our map.

105
00:06:28,234 --> 00:06:31,964
暂停想一想：如果 Alice 的真实答案为“是”
Pause and ponder: if Alice's true answer is yes,

106
00:06:31,964 --> 00:06:35,179
她有多大概率回答“是”？换成“否”呢？
how likely is she to say yes? And if it is no?

107
00:06:48,017 --> 00:06:54,096
真实答案为“是”，她回答“是”的概率是 3/4：正面，或者先反后正
If the truth is yes, she says yes 3/4 of the time: heads, or tails then heads.

108
00:06:54,416 --> 00:06:59,017
换成“否”，只有第二枚硬币能让她回答“是”：1/4
If it is no, only the second coin can say yes: 1/4.

109
00:06:59,337 --> 00:07:02,666
最坏的比值是 3，所以硬币满足定义
The worst ratio is 3, so the coin satisfies the definition,

110
00:07:02,666 --> 00:07:06,582
ε 就等于 3 的自然对数，大约 1.1
with ε = ln 3, about 1.1.

111
00:07:06,817 --> 00:07:09,908
现在你是攻击者，想区分这两个世界
Now be the attacker, trying to tell the two worlds apart.

112
00:07:10,228 --> 00:07:15,496
按贝叶斯公式，后验概率比恰好是先验概率比乘上这个比值
By Bayes' rule, your new odds are your old odds times exactly this ratio,

113
00:07:15,496 --> 00:07:21,672
所以最多只会变成原来的 e^ε 倍，无论你之前知道什么
so they move by at most a factor of e^ε, whatever you knew before.

114
00:07:21,992 --> 00:07:28,935
一开始是五五开的话，ε 取 0.1 最多有 52.5% 的把握
Starting from 50/50, ε = 0.1 leaves you at most 52.5% sure;

115
00:07:28,935 --> 00:07:31,386
取 1 最多 73%
ε = 1, at most 73%.

116
00:07:31,706 --> 00:07:35,564
ε 是人为选定的；原文管它叫 leakage（泄露量）
ε is set by policy; the paper calls it the leakage.

117
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,465
再来看它不保证什么
Notice what this does not promise.

118
00:07:37,785 --> 00:07:40,984
假如研究发现吸烟者更容易得心脏病
If a study reveals that smokers get more heart disease,

119
00:07:40,984 --> 00:07:45,284
而 Alice 吸烟，别人现在就可能觉得她风险更高
and Alice smokes, people may now think she is at higher risk.

120
00:07:45,604 --> 00:07:50,350
这不算侵犯隐私：同样的结论从其他人的数据里也能得出
That is not a privacy violation: the same lesson could be learned from everyone else's data,

121
00:07:50,350 --> 00:07:54,887
所以就算把 Alice 的记录换成别人的，也照样会发生
so it would happen even if Alice's row were replaced by someone else's.

122
00:07:56,333 --> 00:07:59,099
为什么每个输出的比值都要有上界？
Why demand a ratio bound for every single output?

123
00:07:59,419 --> 00:08:02,065
密码学常常满足于更弱的标准
Cryptography often settles for something weaker:

124
00:08:02,065 --> 00:08:05,655
统计距离（即 TV 距离），也就是两条曲线间面积的一半
statistical distance, half the area between the two curves.

125
00:08:05,975 --> 00:08:10,470
等价地说，就是任意事件的概率在两个世界间的最大差距
Equivalently, the most the probability of any event can differ between the worlds.

126
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:13,238
原文说明了它在这里为什么不够
The paper shows why that is not enough here.

127
00:08:13,483 --> 00:08:17,122
看这个机制：随机挑一条记录，原样发布
Consider this mechanism: pick one row at random and publish it, word for word.

128
00:08:17,442 --> 00:08:21,719
改动一个人的记录，输出分布只会变化 1/n
Change one person's row, and the output distribution moves by only 1/n.

129
00:08:22,039 --> 00:08:24,940
数据库很大时这点变化微不足道
For a big database that is tiny,

130
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:29,580
所以按这种平均意义上的度量，它看起来不泄露隐私
so by the averaged measure this looks private.

131
00:08:29,816 --> 00:08:32,666
可每个输出都是某个人的完整记录
But every output is somebody's complete record.

132
00:08:32,986 --> 00:08:37,418
比值这一关能拦住它：显示 Alice 真实取值的输出
The ratio test catches it: the output showing Alice's real value

133
00:08:37,418 --> 00:08:41,069
一个世界里概率是 1/n，另一个是 0
has probability 1/n in one world, and 0 in the other.

134
00:08:41,389 --> 00:08:42,900
比值是无穷大
The ratio is infinite.

135
00:08:42,950 --> 00:08:47,365
平均值会放过那些对每个人来说都很罕见的灾难
Averages let catastrophes slip through, as long as each is rare for any single person.

136
00:08:47,685 --> 00:08:50,585
而比值上界会处处把它们排除在外
A ratio bound rules them out everywhere.

137
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:53,255
它也解答了四舍五入那道题
It also settles our rounding question:

138
00:08:53,255 --> 00:08:58,135
在跳变处，一个世界给出这个答案的概率是 1，另一个是 0
at the jump, one world gives that answer with probability 1, the other with probability 0.

139
00:08:58,455 --> 00:09:01,547
想过这一关，机制就必须是随机的
To pass this test, a mechanism has to be random.

140
00:09:02,983 --> 00:09:04,701
那噪声到底要加多少？
So how much noise do we need?

141
00:09:05,021 --> 00:09:07,709
这只取决于 query 的一个性质
It depends on a single property of the query:

142
00:09:07,709 --> 00:09:12,415
它的敏感度，也就是改变一条记录最多能让答案变化多少
its sensitivity, the most that changing one row can ever change the answer,

143
00:09:12,415 --> 00:09:16,215
取遍每一对相邻数据库，包括还不存在的那些
over all pairs of neighboring databases, including ones that do not exist yet.

144
00:09:16,450 --> 00:09:18,179
对 counting query（计数查询）
For a counting query,

145
00:09:18,179 --> 00:09:21,382
比如医院那个，一条记录最多让答案变 1
like our hospital count, one row changes the answer by at most 1.

146
00:09:21,702 --> 00:09:23,000
敏感度是 1
Sensitivity 1.

147
00:09:23,050 --> 00:09:27,167
再看直方图：把一条记录的可能取值分成 d 个桶
Now a histogram: split the possible values of a row into d bins,

148
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:28,984
发布每个桶的记录数
and release how many rows fall in each.

149
00:09:29,304 --> 00:09:31,831
先别急着看答案，暂停一下
Before I show you, pause:

150
00:09:31,831 --> 00:09:36,466
如果 Alice 的记录变了，整个直方图总共能变多少？
if Alice's row changes, how much can the whole histogram change in total?

151
00:09:36,786 --> 00:09:38,447
这跟桶的数量有关吗？
Does it depend on the number of bins?

152
00:09:47,283 --> 00:09:52,133
她从一个桶搬到另一个桶：一个桶少了 1，另一个桶多了 1
She moves out of one bin and into another: one count goes down by 1, another goes up by 1.

153
00:09:52,453 --> 00:09:54,053
总变化量：2
Total change: 2.

154
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:57,802
像这样把各个分量变化的绝对值加起来
Adding up absolute changes across coordinates like this

155
00:09:57,802 --> 00:10:02,366
就是 L1 范数，原文就用它来衡量一列数的敏感度
is the L1 norm, the paper's way to measure sensitivity for lists of numbers.

156
00:10:02,686 --> 00:10:06,646
而且它总是 2，不管是 5 个桶还是 5000 个桶
And it is 2 whether there are 5 bins or 5000.

157
00:10:06,966 --> 00:10:08,620
它和维度完全无关
It does not depend on the dimension at all.

158
00:10:08,866 --> 00:10:12,028
对比一下：数据库里最高的收入是多少？
Contrast that with: what is the largest income in the database?

159
00:10:12,348 --> 00:10:17,523
一个亿万富翁，就能让答案变动 10 亿，不封顶就根本没有上限
One billionaire can move that answer by $1B, and with no cap there is no limit at all.

160
00:10:17,843 --> 00:10:21,620
标准做法是先给每个值封顶，比如 100 万
The standard fix is to cap every value, say at $1M, first.

161
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:26,918
这个 trick 要记住：差分隐私深度学习对梯度做的就是这个
Remember that trick: it is exactly what private deep learning does to gradients.

162
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:28,570
再强调两点
Two things to remember.

163
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:30,872
敏感度只取决于函数本身
Sensitivity is a property of the function alone,

164
00:10:30,872 --> 00:10:34,438
与具体的数据库无关，也不是人为选定的
not of the particular database, and it is not chosen by policy.

165
00:10:34,758 --> 00:10:36,518
ε 是选出来的
ε is a choice.

166
00:10:36,838 --> 00:10:38,438
敏感度是算出来的
Sensitivity is a fact.

167
00:10:39,817 --> 00:10:41,394
下面来看噪声
Now for the noise.

168
00:10:41,444 --> 00:10:43,874
原文用的是拉普拉斯分布
The paper uses the Laplace distribution:

169
00:10:43,874 --> 00:10:48,736
左右对称，峰很尖，并且随着离中心的距离指数衰减
symmetric, sharply peaked, and falling off exponentially with distance from the center.

170
00:10:49,056 --> 00:10:51,969
它的宽度由尺度参数 λ 决定
Its width is set by a scale parameter, λ.

171
00:10:53,017 --> 00:10:54,617
关键的 trick 来了
Here is the trick.

172
00:10:54,689 --> 00:10:58,992
一条拉普拉斯曲线的中心在 f(x)，也就是 41
Center one Laplace curve at f(x), 41,

173
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:04,905
另一条在 f(x′)，也就是 42：这就是两个世界的输出分布
and another at f(x′), 42: the output distributions of our two worlds.

174
00:11:05,150 --> 00:11:09,279
现在对每个输出 t，画出两条曲线比值的对数
Now plot the log of their ratio for every output t.

175
00:11:09,599 --> 00:11:12,343
在 41 左边，它完全是个常数
To the left of 41, it is exactly constant.

176
00:11:12,663 --> 00:11:14,937
在 42 右边，又是个常数
To the right of 42, constant again.

177
00:11:15,257 --> 00:11:17,220
中间是一段直线斜坡
In between, a straight ramp.

178
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:24,549
它从不超过 1/λ，也从不低于 −1/λ：也就是平移量除以尺度
It never rises above 1/λ, and never falls below −1/λ: the shift, divided by the scale.

179
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:29,523
为什么？取对数之后，拉普拉斯密度是个帐篷形
Why? On a log scale, a Laplace density is a tent,

180
00:11:29,523 --> 00:11:33,276
两边的斜率是 1/λ，绝不会更陡
whose sides have slope 1/λ, never steeper.

181
00:11:33,596 --> 00:11:36,561
把帐篷平移过去，两个帐篷的高度差
Slide the tent over, and the gap between the tents

182
00:11:36,561 --> 00:11:39,177
永远不超过平移量乘以这个斜率
can never exceed the slide times that slope.

183
00:11:39,497 --> 00:11:45,043
这就是整个设计原则：隐私需要的噪声，对数密度必须处处不陡
That is the whole design principle: privacy needs noise whose log density is never steep.

184
00:11:45,784 --> 00:11:51,157
用符号写出来：t 到两个中心的距离，最多相差中心之间的距离
In symbols: two distances to t can differ by at most the distance between the centers.

185
00:11:51,477 --> 00:11:56,252
所以任意输出的隐私损失，最多是敏感度除以 λ
So the privacy loss of any output is at most the sensitivity divided by λ.

186
00:11:56,572 --> 00:12:02,966
让 λ 取敏感度除以 ε，比值就始终在 e^ε 以内
Set λ to the sensitivity over ε, and the ratio stays within e^ε,

187
00:12:02,966 --> 00:12:06,535
对任意输出、任意一对相邻数据库都成立
for every output and every pair of neighbors.

188
00:12:06,855 --> 00:12:09,188
隐私，一个不等式就证完了
Privacy, proven in one line.

189
00:12:09,434 --> 00:12:14,998
如果 query 返回好几个数，就给每个数加上独立的拉普拉斯噪声
If the query returns several numbers, add independent Laplace noise to each.

190
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:18,376
这时联合密度取决于 L1 距离
The joint density then depends on the L1 distance,

191
00:12:18,376 --> 00:12:22,512
正因为这样，敏感度才用 L1 范数来衡量
which is exactly why sensitivity is measured in the L1 norm.

192
00:12:22,832 --> 00:12:29,661
这就是命题 1：在每个分量上加尺度为 S(f)/ε 的拉普拉斯噪声
That is Proposition 1: Laplace noise of scale S(f)/ε in every coordinate.

193
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:32,923
暂停想一想：为什么不用更简单的
Pause and ponder: why not something simpler,

194
00:12:32,923 --> 00:12:36,324
比如在 −10 到 +10 之间均匀分布的噪声？
like uniform noise anywhere between −10 and +10?

195
00:12:47,167 --> 00:12:48,365
看看边缘
Look at the edges.

196
00:12:48,415 --> 00:12:53,545
输出 51.5，真实人数是 42 就可能，是 41 就不可能
An output of 51.5 is possible if the true count is 42 but impossible if it is 41:

197
00:12:53,545 --> 00:12:59,664
又是那个无穷大比值，随机发布一条记录的机制当初就栽在这上面
the same infinite ratio that sank the random-row mechanism.

198
00:12:59,984 --> 00:13:03,383
好的噪声，绝不能把任何输出排除在外
Good noise must never rule an output out.

199
00:13:03,617 --> 00:13:06,116
那为什么不用熟悉的钟形曲线？
And why not the familiar bell curve?

200
00:13:06,436 --> 00:13:10,530
取对数之后，高斯是一条抛物线，越来越陡
On a log scale a Gaussian is a parabola, steeper and steeper,

201
00:13:10,530 --> 00:13:14,830
所以两条平移开的抛物线，高度差会无限增大
so the gap between two shifted parabolas grows without bound.

202
00:13:15,150 --> 00:13:19,154
到了尾部，比值会爆炸，没有哪个 ε 能管用
In the tails the ratio explodes, and no single ε works.

203
00:13:19,474 --> 00:13:21,407
不过先记住这个高斯
Hold on to that Gaussian, though:

204
00:13:21,407 --> 00:13:26,629
它还会回来，用差分隐私训练神经网络时，实际用的就是它
it comes back, and it is the noise you would actually use to train a neural network privately.

205
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:33,486
这就是标题里说的按敏感度校准噪声：噪声尺度等于敏感度除以 ε
So here is the recipe in the title: noise scale equals sensitivity divided by ε.

206
00:13:33,806 --> 00:13:36,388
敏感度越高的 query，噪声越大
A more sensitive question needs more noise.

207
00:13:36,708 --> 00:13:38,820
隐私越强，噪声越大
Stronger privacy needs more noise.

208
00:13:40,367 --> 00:13:45,770
回到医院的例子，ε 取 0.5：尺度为 2 的拉普拉斯噪声
Back to the hospital, with ε = 0.5: Laplace noise of scale 2.

209
00:13:46,090 --> 00:13:49,510
第一周，管理者报出大约 43.7
Week 1, the curator reports about 43.7.

210
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:54,031
第二周，真实人数是 42，报出大约 40.6
Week 2, when the true count is 42, about 40.6.

211
00:13:54,351 --> 00:13:58,347
跟之前一样做减法，Alice 好像让人数少了 3
Subtract as before, and Alice seems to have lowered the count by 3.

212
00:13:58,667 --> 00:14:04,166
原本对她的判断是五五开，现在最多能有大约 62% 的把握
A 50/50 guess about her can now move to at most about 62%.

213
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:08,505
再看噪声尺度取决于什么：敏感度和 ε
Now look at what the noise scale depends on: the sensitivity and ε.

214
00:14:08,825 --> 00:14:10,511
而不是数据库的规模
Not the size of the database.

215
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:16,088
有 100 个病人时，噪声一般在 2 左右，占答案的百分之几
With 100 patients, noise of typical size 2 is a few percent of the answer.

216
00:14:16,408 --> 00:14:19,678
到了 100 万人，这点噪声可以忽略不计
With a million, it is a rounding error.

217
00:14:19,998 --> 00:14:25,313
保护 Alice 的噪声，比起她自己的贡献，也就是 1，算是很大
Alice is protected by noise that is large compared to her own contribution, which is 1,

218
00:14:25,313 --> 00:14:27,149
但比起总体微不足道
but tiny compared to the population's.

219
00:14:28,384 --> 00:14:30,180
隐私，留给个体
Privacy for individuals.

220
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,163
准确，留给总体
Accuracy for populations.

221
00:14:32,483 --> 00:14:34,405
这就是差分隐私的取舍
That is the bargain.

222
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:36,627
这一题你可以自己回答
Here is one you can answer yourself.

223
00:14:36,947 --> 00:14:40,948
暂停想一想：噪声大约有 1/ε 那么大
Pause and ponder: the noise has size about 1/ε.

224
00:14:41,268 --> 00:14:45,338
如果 ε 远小于 1/n，会出什么问题？
What goes wrong if ε is much smaller than 1/n?

225
00:14:58,184 --> 00:15:03,685
噪声超过了 n，比人数可能取到的任何值都大，答案成了纯噪声
The noise outgrows n, bigger than the count could ever be, and the answer is pure noise.

226
00:15:04,005 --> 00:15:06,129
这不是拉普拉斯噪声的问题
This is not Laplace's fault.

227
00:15:06,449 --> 00:15:12,284
任意两个数据库之间，都有一条最多 n 步的链，每步只改一条记录
Any two databases are linked by a chain of at most n single-row changes,

228
00:15:12,284 --> 00:15:19,509
概率之比最多是 e^ε，所以两端之比最多是 e^(nε)
each changing probabilities by at most e^ε, so the ends differ by at most e^(nε).

229
00:15:19,829 --> 00:15:25,381
如果 nε 极小，所有数据库看起来都一样，什么也学不到
If nε is tiny, every database looks alike, and nothing can be learned.

230
00:15:25,701 --> 00:15:28,751
这种链式 trick 叫 hybrid argument（混合论证）
This chain trick is called a hybrid argument,

231
00:15:28,751 --> 00:15:30,351
最后还会再出现
and it comes back at the end.
